            ("2.2", ["sf-pd1", "design"], "A trigger must update related records when an Opportunity closes. Related records span 500+ parents. Best approach?", ["Collect parent Ids, query related records once, update in bulk outside loops", "SOQL inside loop for each Opportunity", "Individual update DML per parent in the loop", "Disable the trigger and use reports"], [0], "Standard bulk pattern: gather keys, single query, build map, single DML update list."),
            ("2.2", ["sf-pd1", "design"], "When must logic run asynchronously after commit to avoid mixed DML errors with setup objects?", ["When updating both setup entities (User, Group) and non-setup entities in related logic", "Never; mixed DML is allowed", "Only in Visualforce", "Only in LWC"], [0], "Mixed DML restrictions require async separation or System.runAs patterns when touching setup and non-setup objects."),
            ("2.2", ["sf-pd1", "flows"], "Can a before-delete record-triggered Flow access $Record?", ["Yes, before-delete flows can reference the record being deleted", "No, delete flows only run after commit", "Only with Apex plugins", "Only for Account"], [0], "Record-triggered flows support before-delete and after-delete with access to the triggering record."),
            ("2.2", ["sf-pd1", "async"], "In the finish method of a Batch job, what is a common pattern?", ["Enqueue a Queueable job or send completion notification email", "Query all org users synchronously without limits", "Run unlimited callouts in a loop", "Perform before-trigger logic"], [0], "finish() runs once after all batches complete — ideal for chaining jobs or notifications."),
            ("2.2", ["sf-pd1", "triggers"], "Which scenario requires an 'after' trigger instead of 'before'?", ["Creating related child records that need the parent Id", "Modifying fields on the same record before validation", "Preventing duplicate names on the same record", "Normalizing a field before save"], [0], "Related record creation needs the parent Id assigned after insert, so after triggers (or after insert) are appropriate."),
